# PART 10 — UX AND DESIGN QUALITY REQUIREMENTS

The portfolio must be beautiful, but it must also be easy to use.

Follow these principles:

1. Clear information hierarchy.
2. Consistent navigation.
3. Easy access to projects and experience.
4. Strong readability.
5. Good contrast.
6. Responsive layouts.
7. Arabic RTL support.
8. Consistent component behavior.
9. Purposeful animations only.
10. Reduced-motion accessibility.
11. Clear case-study navigation.
12. No excessive visual clutter.

The storytelling must support the content, not hide it.

Every illustration must have a reason to exist.

Every section must communicate something meaningful.

Do not turn the whole website into a sequence of decorative images with tiny unreadable text.

